(*Spinal Graph*)


(* ::Text:: *)
(*A simple directed graph on a set of nodes.*)


(* ::Text:: *)
(*Spinal graphs allow to encode a (partial) sequential structure of a set of nodes. The target is to have sufficient expressive power to recover common data structures, such as tuples, cycles or trees, as well as more general combinatorial species, while remaining compact and rewriting-friendly. In particular, symmetry properties of data structures should be encoded implicitly. Spinal graphs are a sort of generalized permutation generator.*)


(* ::Text:: *)
(*Chemical Analogy: spinal graphs determine the type of bond among a collection of atoms.*)


